@flexiarg math-formalization/normalize-meromorphic-point-values-before-continuation
@title Normalize Meromorphic Point Values Before Any Continuation Argument
@sigils [🧽/正]
@keywords toMeromorphicNFOn, MeromorphicNFAt, meromorphicOrderAt_toMeromorphicNFOn, meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_iff_analyticAt, toMeromorphicNFAt_eq_self, removable singularity, statement repair, EqOn
@audience lean-provers, complex-analysis
@tone heuristic
@difficulty intermediate
@subjects complex-analysis
@instantiates math-informal/construct-auxiliary-object
@see-also math-formalization/compact-thickening-upgrades-pointwise-analyticity math-formalization/additive-principal-parts-from-order-germs
@examples a95J04

! conclusion:
  A function that is `MeromorphicOn f D` may take arbitrary values at its
  removable points, so `AnalyticAt ℂ f z` — and any lemma asserting
  holomorphy of the raw `f` past a boundary — is false as stated. Pass to
  the normal form `toMeromorphicNFOn f D` first, transfer orders, and carry
  an `EqOn` with `f` on the region where `f` was already analytic.

  + IF: A bridge statement asks for `DifferentiableOn ℂ f (ball 0 R)` or
    `f z = g z + …` beyond the original holomorphic disk, with `f` known
    only as `MeromorphicOn` there.

  + HOWEVER: The statement cannot be proved for the raw `f`; attempts to
    derive `AnalyticAt` from nonnegative order stall because order controls
    a germ off the point, not the value at it.

  + THEN: Restate for `g := toMeromorphicNFOn f D` (the pinned top-level
    theorem is unchanged; bridge lemmas are scaffolding). Use
    `meromorphicNFOn_toMeromorphicNFOn f D hzD : MeromorphicNFAt g z`,
    `hnf.meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_iff_analyticAt`, and
    `meromorphicOrderAt_toMeromorphicNFOn hmero hzD` to turn order facts
    about `f` into analyticity of `g`; prove
    `Set.EqOn g f (ball 0 1)` by `simp [toMeromorphicNFOn, hmero, hzD,
    toMeromorphicNFAt_eq_self.2 han.meromorphicNFAt]`, and feed the
    top-level theorem with `g` plus the `EqOn`.
    + LEAN:
      api[toMeromorphicNFOn] api[meromorphicNFOn_toMeromorphicNFOn]
      api[MeromorphicNFAt.meromorphicOrderAt_nonneg_iff_analyticAt]
      api[meromorphicOrderAt_toMeromorphicNFOn] api[toMeromorphicNFAt_eq_self]

  + BECAUSE: The normal form repairs exactly the point-value defect and
    nothing else, so every order-based statement transfers verbatim and
    every downstream use on the original disk is recovered by the `EqOn`.
